    {
      "time": 1789494139.446466,
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "No credential helper is configured at all \u2014 that's why Git asks for your token every single push. Let's fix that.",
      "id": "3e3d03cb-49d7-4152-bfa5-36d26abd87e9"
    },
    {
      "type": "msg",
      "id": "ca26c846-6418-4422-8a3b-67cc3a96601d",
      "raw_time": false,
      "mentions": [],
      "time": 1789494139.8073242,
      "metadata": {
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "raw_output": "Exit code 127\ngit version 2.34.1\n/bin/bash: line 5: gh: command not found",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_018scw4KX3joSMz3T5d91iRq",
            "raw_input": {
              "description": "Check git version and gh CLI auth status",
              "command": "git --version\nwhich gh 2>&1\ngh auth status 2>&1"
            },
            "permission_status": "resolved",
            "status": "failed",
            "kind": "execute",
            "title": "git --version which gh 2>&1 gh auth status 2>&1",
            "selected_option_id": "allow-once",
            "session_id": "191bb292-282c-46ef-ba8c-c5df114afb05",
            "permission_options": [
              {
                "option_id": "allow-once",
                "kind": "allow_once",
                "name": "Yes"
              },
              {
                "name": "Yes, and don't ask again for git --version and gh auth * commands",
                "kind": "allow_always",
                "option_id": "allow-with-updates"
              },
              {
                "kind": "reject_once",
                "name": "No",
                "option_id": "reject"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "body": "",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
    },
    {
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "No `gh` CLI here, so the simplest fix is Git's built-in credential store. You have two options:\n\n1. **`store`** \u2014 caches the token in plaintext at `~/.git-credentials` permanently (until you change your token/password).\n2. **`cache`** \u2014 caches in memory only for a timeout (default 15 min), then asks again.\n\nGiven this is a persistent JupyterHub-style container, `store` is the practical choice. Want me to run:\n\n```\ngit config --global credential.helper store\n```\n\nThen the *next* push will still ask for your token once, but after that it'll be saved in `~/.git-credentials` and you won't be prompted again. Confirm and I'll set it up.",
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "id": "80a86419-5f00-4efe-b4f6-7cb6686a8c99",
      "time": 1789494148.3940382,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona"
    },
